    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>New package: falcosecurity-container-plugin 0.7.1

The falcosecurity container plugin (libcontainer.so), unbundled from the
copy in sysdig/falco. C++ plugin with a vendored Go worker; loaded at
runtime by the system libsinsp.

INTERDEPENDENT REQUESTS - please stage together (this package will not
build until these land):
  * sr#1360103 - plugin-sdk-cpp (new, build dep)
  * sr#1360178 - re-flex 6.0.0 (build dep; adds the shared libreflex.so.6
    this package links - current Factory re-flex ships no linkable lib)
  * sr#1360164 - falco-libs (runtime: the libsinsp that loads the plugin)
  * sr#1360104 - bshoshany-thread-pool (pulled in via falco-libs)</comment>
    <requestid>1360182</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="2" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>cf943531e7dbe0dd32a87b08f8850413</srcmd5>
    <version>0.7.2</version>
    <time>1788880056</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Update to version 0.7.2:
  * Recognize systemd nerdctl cgroup paths
  * Resubscribe to the CRI container events stream and reset
    the backoff after a healthy subscription
  * Link libresolv on Linux so libcontainer.so loads on
    glibc &lt; 2.34
  * Migrate the Go worker to go.podman.io/podman/v6 and
    containerd v2.2.5 (Podman API floor still 4.0.0)
  * Rebase container-plugin-use-system-deps.patch for the
    new go-worker.cmake resolv hunk
- License: Apache-2.0 AND MPL-2.0 (vendored Go modules
  go-pathrs, filepath-securejoin, hashicorp/errwrap and
  go-multierror)</comment>
    <requestid>1376283</requestid>
  </revision>
